{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/alter"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLHarmonyAlterV","text":"MXLHarmonyAlter"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLNumeralV5alterAA15MXLHarmonyAlterVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","title":"alter"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/alter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLHarmonyAlterV","text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyAlter"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"code":"<numeral-alter>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral-alter element represents an alteration to the numeral-root, similar to the alter element for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pitch. The print-object attribute can be used to hide an alteration in cases such as when the MusicXML"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoding of a 6 or 7 numeral-root in a minor key requires an alteration that is not displayed. The location"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute indicates whether the alteration should appear to the left or the right of the numeral-root. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left by default."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumeral","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumeral","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral type represents the Roman numeral or Nashville number part of a harmony. It requires that the key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be specified in the encoding, either with a key or numeral-key element."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumeral","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/alter":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLHarmonyAlterV","text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/alter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"alter","abstract":[{"text":"The numeral-alter element represents an alteration to the numeral-root, similar to the alter element for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pitch. The print-object attribute can be used to hide an alteration in cases such as when the MusicXML","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"encoding of a 6 or 7 numeral-root in a minor key requires an alteration that is not displayed. The location","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"attribute indicates whether the alteration should appear to the left or the right of the numeral-root. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left by default.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/alter"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmonyAlter":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmonyAlter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLHarmonyAlter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLHarmonyAlter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The harmony-alter type represents the chromatic alteration of the root, numeral, or bass of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"harmony-chord group within the harmony element. In some chord styles, the text of the preceding element may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"include alteration information. In that case, the print-object attribute of this type can be set to no. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"location attribute indicates whether the alteration should appear to the left or the right of the preceding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. Its default value varies by element."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmonyalter"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}